WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.700
An attorney

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.134
for former

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.569
President Trump blames

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.537
the media for Trump's claim

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.406
that he'll be arrested on Tuesday

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.540
in Manhattan.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.076
In a statement to CNN, Joe Tacopina says

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.778
No one tells us anything,

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.246
which is very frustrating.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:15.315
President Trump is basing his response

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.816
on press reports

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:17.550
and the fact

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.619
that this is a political prosecution

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:20.587
and the D.A.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.188
leaks things to the press

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.090
instead of communicating to the lawyers,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.291
as they should.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.926
Now, this drama began

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:27.727
earlier today

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.763
on Trump's truth, a social page

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.499
after predicting his arrest on Tuesday.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.801
The former president urged his supporters

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.970
to, quote, take back our nation.

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:38.071
And tonight,

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.473
his campaign is already fundraise

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:41.574
off of his claims,

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.376
which have not been confirmed.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.277
There's no indication

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.112
that he will be arrested Tuesday.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:46.579
Now, sources

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.748
tell me and my colleague Kristen Holmes

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.550
that Trump's legal team has gotten

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.052
no word from the Manhattan

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.553
district attorney's office

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.487
about the timing

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.222
of any possible indictment.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.425
Another source says the former president

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.326
has been pushing his team

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:03.463
to get the base riled up over the idea

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:04.831
because he believes

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.566
it would help him politically.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:07.500
CNN's Caitlin

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.601
Polanco is following

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.270
the latest developments

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.472
in this long time investigation

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.274
into possible hush money payments.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.177
Paula, Donald Trump

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:17.777
does say

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.045
that he is expecting

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:19.712
to be arrested

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.413
on Tuesday

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:21.748
in Manhattan in this ongoing

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.583
financial crimes investigation,

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.818
but he actually doesn't

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.953
know at this point in time.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.089
A spokesperson for Trump

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.490
said this morning in a statement

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.024
that there has been

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.759
no indication formally

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:33.660
from the Manhattan

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.195
district attorney's office

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:36.963
that Trump is about to be indicted

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:37.997
or arrested.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.866
However, we do know that

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.435
this ongoing investigation into possible

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.837
financial crimes

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:45.672
may be falsification of business

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:47.207
records of the Trump Organization,

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.541
all connecting

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:52.212
back to that $130,000 payment

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.813
that Trump's lawyer, Michael Cohen,

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:56.983
made to Stormy Daniels to cover up things

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:57.517
that she wanted

00:01:57.517 --> 00:02:00.153
to allege in his 2016 campaign.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.455
All of that investigation

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.556
is nearing the end

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:06.025
because Trump was invited to testify,

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.994
which he had the right to do.

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.229
He declined to do that.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:10.263
That is the sort of thing

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:11.631
that happens at the very end

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.766
of a grand jury investigation like this.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:14.701
But we do know

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:15.768
that there is another witness

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:18.204
coming into the grand jury on Monday.

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.340
At least scheduled to be testifying.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.075
And so at this point in time,

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:23.843
we don't know exactly when

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:24.644
or exactly

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:27.180
what charges may be approved

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.215
or may be asked to be approved

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.683
by the grand jury

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:31.751
sitting in Manhattan

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:34.621
in this unprecedented investigation

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.789
that could lead to a criminal charge

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.324
against the former president

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.093
of the United States Paula.

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.229
Caitlin, Paul, Lance, thank you.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:44.164
Meantime, sources

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.332
tell CNN that meetings have been going on

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.100
throughout the week

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:47.834
among city,

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.702
state and federal law enforcement

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.404
agencies in New York

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.173
about security preparations

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.542
in case Trump's predictions are correct.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:58.011
CNN's Polo Sandoval is outside

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:58.578
the Manhattan

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.413
Criminal Courthouse with more.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.681
Polo, CNN has learned

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.250
that NYPD officials were briefed

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.353
on security measures today

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:08.955
Yeah, Polo,

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.390
these law enforcement officials

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.257
that are engaged in these

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:12.992
ongoing behind the scenes

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.061
conversations telling CNN

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.197
that there are some concerns

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.231
that they've raised.

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:19.632
When should or at least

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.100
should we reach that point

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:21.734
where Donald Trump

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:22.669
would have to come here

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:23.536
to lower Manhattan

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:25.305
to answer to any potential charges?

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:26.673
And among those concerns

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.608
would certainly be courthouse security.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:28.942
A reminder,

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:31.444
we do live in a post January 6th World.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.045
And so

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.246
there are certainly concerns

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:35.648
about the potential for demonstrations

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:36.683
or rallies

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:37.917
by Trump supporters

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.786
and that today's message

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:41.020
from the former president

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.188
could further galvanize them

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:44.557
to take them beyond just peaceful protest

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.726
and then resulting

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:47.927
counterprotest, perhaps.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.062
And that is why local, state

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:49.862
and federal officials,

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.364
according to several sources

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.465
speaking to CNN,

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.000
are having these conversations

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.568
about how they would respond.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:56.703
Another just fascinating

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.537
wrinkle in all of this,

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:57.971
Paula, is

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.038
what one federal source

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.673
told our colleague, John Miller,

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.041
that the former president's

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:02.742
Secret Service

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:03.843
protective detail

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.778
is also engaged in conversations

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.480
with fellow agents here in New York City

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.782
about what the logistics would look like

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.252
in terms of transporting Donald Trump

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:13.620
to the region

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.687
here, to the Manhattan

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.756
district attorney's office to respond

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:17.023
or at least

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:18.691
to face any potential charges

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.160
and go through the booking process

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:22.395
just like any other way,

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.863
which would include

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.498
fingerprinting, mug shot

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:27.400
photos being taken and, of course

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.869
the eventual eventual arraignment

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.137
of a defendant,

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:31.704
obviously

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.172
because of the attention on this.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.741
It is expected that this would be

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:35.475
this would happen away

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.143
from crowds, away from cameras.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.177
But we'll certainly have to see,

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:38.444
of course,

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:39.646
should we arrive at that point.

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:41.047
But it just goes to speak

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.749
to the fascinating and unprecedented

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.250
nature of the behind

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.518
the scenes conversations

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:46.953
that are happening among

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.121
those are obviously coming from

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:48.921
law enforcement

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.256
that are

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:51.891
trying to sort of forecast

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:52.925
where we would be

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.027
should we reach that point.

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:54.394
Of course,

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:55.862
we're talking about charges being filed

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:58.231
against the former president Paula.

00:04:58.231 --> 00:04:59.532
Polo Sandoval, thank you

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:02.001
And joining

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:02.402
us now,

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.170
CNN national security analyst

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.138
Juliette Kayyem.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:07.373
She's also a former assistant secretary

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:09.442
at the Department of Homeland Security.

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:10.443
Juliette, of course,

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.412
calling for protests is legal,

00:05:12.412 --> 00:05:14.213
protected by the First Amendment.

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:15.181
But how much does

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.849
the specter of January six

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:18.051
hang over

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:18.785
Trump's latest

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:20.453
remarks calling for protest,

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:22.221
protest protests?

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:22.789
Right.

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:24.724
Even before January six,

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:25.858
Trump became an expert

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:26.759
or was an expert

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.328
in using language

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:30.797
to incite without actually directing it.

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:32.365
I mean, even for January six,

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:34.801
it was clear what he wanted to happen.

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.069
But he never said,

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:39.272
you know, storm Congress and and lose.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:40.440
And I think

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.874
actually the language in his statement

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.776
this morning,

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.745
what was less troublesome is protest.

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:46.446
That's fine.

00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:48.614
Where democracy was his

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.049
take America back language.

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:52.285
That's directly from January six.

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:54.020
But the language that he used on

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.621
January six, somehow

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:58.858
something's being taken away from me.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:00.660
And I have to fight

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.995
essentially with violence to get it back.

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:06.032
But the the times have changed

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:09.068
and and Trump will begin to realize that.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:10.536
I mean, one is he's not in power.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:11.871
So we can't direct

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.806
law enforcement agencies.

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:15.074
Hundreds of people are in jail

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:15.908
or been indicted.

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:19.512
He he cannot promise to pardon people.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:21.314
Law enforcement, as we're reporting,

00:06:21.314 --> 00:06:22.682
is clearly on notice.

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:25.351
And and he's thrown out this Tuesday day.

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:26.386
I kind of doubt it.

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:27.620
I don't know

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.321
if they're

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.423
honestly following their interviewing

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:32.125
a witness on Monday.

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:34.494
The Tuesday date is probably Trump

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:38.097
wanting to have us all look at Tuesday.

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:38.965
It doesn't happen.

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:41.033
And him saying look, they don't have it.

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.769
So we just wait

00:06:42.769 --> 00:06:45.104
until there's actually movement.

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:46.139
You make a great point.

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:46.672
And again,

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:47.440
our reporting is

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.108
there is no indication

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:50.743
that there is an arrest on Tuesday.

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:52.245
His team hasn't been told that.

00:06:52.245 --> 00:06:53.146
And as we've been reporting,

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:54.781
there's a witness coming Monday.

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:55.615
But as Trump calls

00:06:55.615 --> 00:06:56.349
for the protests,

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:58.084
the House speaker, Kevin McCarthy,

00:06:58.084 --> 00:06:59.552
he's got on Twitter to say

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:00.253
any arrest

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.020
would be, quote,

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:01.821
an outrageous

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.956
abuse of power by a radical D.A.

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:06.192
who lets violent criminals walk

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:08.161
as he pursues political vengeance

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:10.029
against President Trump.

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:11.564
Now, how do those remarks play?

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:12.064
Because really, he's

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:13.032
talking about

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:14.233
the potentially politically

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:15.968
motivated prosecution.

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.069
But Trump is calling for people

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:19.539
to take back the country to the streets

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:20.106
Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:21.874
You can't reconcile with that, really.

00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:22.375
Right.

00:07:22.375 --> 00:07:25.778
And I found McCarthy McCarthy's statement

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:26.546
pretty weak.

00:07:26.546 --> 00:07:28.414
I mean, I know people get upset by them,

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:30.082
but so you're going to have a hearing.

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:30.650
Like what aren't

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.518
they having a hearing about, actually?

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:33.386
I mean, look,

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:34.320
I found a week

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.556
I sort of viewed it as performative,

00:07:36.556 --> 00:07:38.057
like he sort of has to do this.

00:07:38.057 --> 00:07:39.625
But if you're Trump

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.260
and the speaker of the House

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.895
in your party

00:07:42.895 --> 00:07:44.530
is not saying

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.231
what you would

00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:46.632
probably want him to say,

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.367
which is not just that it's outrageous,

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:50.369
but people should protest and

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:51.604
protect Trump.

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:53.506
You're going to be a little bit nervous.

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:54.574
And I think that's

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:55.441
I think it's

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:58.344
I think we we sometimes look at the smoke

00:07:58.344 --> 00:07:59.679
and all the people yelling

00:07:59.679 --> 00:08:01.414
and Fox News and think,

00:08:01.414 --> 00:08:02.348
oh, you know,

00:08:02.348 --> 00:08:03.950
obviously Trump is still popular,

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:04.951
but everyone's

00:08:04.951 --> 00:08:06.018
going to take to the streets.

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:06.686
And even worse,

00:08:06.686 --> 00:08:09.121
some of them will take to arms.

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:11.691
And I think if you just sort of look back

00:08:11.691 --> 00:08:13.359
since January six,

00:08:13.359 --> 00:08:15.027
there's tremendous amount of evidence

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:15.495
as well

00:08:15.495 --> 00:08:17.497
that that that was the peak

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:19.732
and that he's just not able

00:08:19.732 --> 00:08:21.067
essentially to fill a room.

00:08:21.067 --> 00:08:22.001
Look at C-PAC

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:22.502
when you've got you

00:08:22.502 --> 00:08:22.902
what we were

00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:25.071
reporting on CPAC last weekend.

00:08:25.071 --> 00:08:26.572
He can't fill a room

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:28.741
where people pay to see him. So.

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:30.810
So I'm you know,

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:31.110
I mean,

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.011
I think that

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:33.145
McCarthy's statement,

00:08:33.145 --> 00:08:35.681
again, was performative.

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:35.948
Well,

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:37.950
let's talk about the security concerns.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.318
If there is an indictment,

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:40.653
if he does go in person

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:42.455
for his initial appearance

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:43.356
as someone who's worked

00:08:43.356 --> 00:08:44.724
at the Department of Homeland Security.

00:08:44.724 --> 00:08:45.057
Yeah.

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:46.592
What kind of things are you looking at?

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:49.762
Because that courthouse on an average day

00:08:49.996 --> 00:08:52.098
is a circus with high profile defendants,

00:08:52.098 --> 00:08:53.432
as I'm sure you know.

00:08:53.432 --> 00:08:54.534
There is paparazzi,

00:08:54.534 --> 00:08:55.568
there's foreign press.

00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:58.237
It can be quite quite chaotic.

00:08:58.571 --> 00:08:59.939
What are they looking at

00:08:59.939 --> 00:09:00.406
with the idea

00:09:00.406 --> 00:09:01.440
of a former president

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.608
possibly showing up there

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:03.876
for an arraignment?

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:04.310
Right.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.078
So there's all the different pieces

00:09:06.078 --> 00:09:06.712
are going to happen.

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:08.114
In different locations as well.

00:09:08.114 --> 00:09:09.415
So first, I just,

00:09:09.415 --> 00:09:09.916
you know,

00:09:10.116 --> 00:09:11.050
follow the threat

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:12.151
stream, the intelligence stream.

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:13.085
We don't know if other things

00:09:13.085 --> 00:09:14.820
might happen in other cities as well.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.522
So first,

00:09:16.522 --> 00:09:17.690
this is the Secret Service,

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:20.526
which is put in in a historic position,

00:09:20.526 --> 00:09:20.860
which is

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:22.595
they would have to deliver the body

00:09:22.595 --> 00:09:24.497
of the president essentially

00:09:24.497 --> 00:09:26.832
to a new courthouse so

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:28.501
and there's always been speculation

00:09:28.501 --> 00:09:30.603
about the extent to which in the past

00:09:30.603 --> 00:09:33.506
that group of presidential detailees

00:09:33.506 --> 00:09:34.707
had been sort of

00:09:34.707 --> 00:09:35.975
taken with Trump

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:38.311
that has changed over time.

00:09:38.311 --> 00:09:40.446
And I suspect that there is

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:42.348
there is a lot of focus on

00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:43.916
who the personnel will be

00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:44.951
over in New York.

00:09:44.951 --> 00:09:48.387
You're going to have a control,

00:09:49.155 --> 00:09:51.090
geographic control of the courtroom.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:54.226
I do not mean to make this analogy.

00:09:54.226 --> 00:09:55.895
It's just a helpful one.

00:09:55.895 --> 00:09:57.597
This courthouse knows

00:09:57.597 --> 00:10:00.766
how to prepare for defendants.

00:10:00.766 --> 00:10:01.701
It was preparing

00:10:01.701 --> 00:10:03.302
for Guantanamo defendants.

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:03.936
It has had high

00:10:03.936 --> 00:10:05.738
profile terrorism defendants

00:10:05.738 --> 00:10:07.039
Trump is not one of them.

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:08.641
This is a different kind of case.

00:10:08.641 --> 00:10:10.209
It knows how to do this

00:10:10.209 --> 00:10:11.711
with with the NYPD.

00:10:11.711 --> 00:10:13.746
They know how to control

00:10:13.746 --> 00:10:15.414
the the area around it

00:10:15.414 --> 00:10:17.783
and then also those who

00:10:17.783 --> 00:10:19.885
who legitimately have access to it.

00:10:20.086 --> 00:10:21.120
My biggest concern is,

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:22.388
of course, for the people

00:10:22.388 --> 00:10:24.457
who are prosecuting this case,

00:10:24.457 --> 00:10:26.025
they will have increased

00:10:26.025 --> 00:10:27.660
security details as well.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.362
They are more vulnerable

00:10:29.362 --> 00:10:29.862
because they're just

00:10:29.862 --> 00:10:31.364
human beings doing their job

00:10:31.364 --> 00:10:32.565
and they have families

00:10:32.565 --> 00:10:33.699
and things like that.

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:35.635
So those are sort of the three areas

00:10:35.635 --> 00:10:38.070
that the security will be looking at.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:38.771
And we'll see if there

00:10:38.771 --> 00:10:40.539
actually is an indictment and if it comes

00:10:40.539 --> 00:10:41.240
this week.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.508
Juliette Kayyem, thank you so much.

